# Deny by default, then re-allow exactly what the image needs.
#
# The previous version was an allow-by-default list of five entries, which
# meant anything new was shipped unless someone remembered to exclude it.
# Two things were already leaking through it:
#
#   .env   -- carries GROQ_API_KEY. `COPY . .` baked it into an image
#             layer, where it survives regardless of what the running
#             container's environment says, and is readable by anyone who
#             can pull the image.
#   data/  -- 185 MB of uploaded footage and renders at time of writing,
#             copied into every build.
#
# Inverting the default is what stops the next one silently repeating it.
*

# --- what the build actually needs ------------------------------------
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!alembic.ini
!backend/
!docker/entrypoint.sh
# Not documentation as far as the build is concerned: pyproject.toml
# declares `readme = "README.md"`, so hatchling fails the wheel build with
# `OSError: Readme file does not exist` without it.
!README.md

# --- re-exclude things that live under the paths above -----------------
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/

# Secrets: never in an image layer. Configuration is injected at run time
# (env vars / --env-file), which is also what lets one image serve local,
# staging and production without a rebuild. Redundant given the `*` above,
# and kept anyway -- this is the line that must not be deleted by accident.
**/.env
**/.env.*
